  "reasoning": "The claim that humans only use 10% of their brain capacity is a widespread and long-debunked urban legend. Modern neuroimaging techniques, such as functional MRI (fMRI) and PET scans, show that virtually all parts of the brain are active throughout the day, even during simple tasks or sleep. Furthermore, evolutionary neuroscience indicates that if 90% of the brain were unused, brain damage to those dormant areas would carry no consequence, yet damage to almost any region of the brain leads to functional deficits. Brain tissue that goes completely unused also naturally atrophies or degenerates. Scientific consensus unanimously classifies the 10% claim as a myth.",
